  "summary": "Recent preprints and publications pair graph and image encodings with cell-line context to model drug synergy and toxicity endpoints.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is multimodal representation learning for molecular and drug-combination prediction, with graph-based models as the common backbone. SynCell builds a unified graph linking drugs, proteins, PPI relations and cell lines, applying graph convolution to contextualize synergy prediction by cell line. CHMR uses hierarchical multimodal representations with tree-structured vector quantization to jointly model molecules and cellular responses for molecular property prediction. BTP-MFFGNN fuses molecular fingerprints with graph features for drug-induced osteotoxicity, reporting ACC 0.85 and AUC 0.92. SynergyImage departs from graph encoding, representing drug structures as ImageMol images and cell-line gene expression as DeepInsight images. The new elements are explicit cell-line conditioning in SynCell and CHMR and image-based encoding in SynergyImage, while combining complementary representations of molecules and biological context remains the shared design choice.",
